`comment("Detection: Privilege Escalation / New Admin Account Creation")`
`comment("Sourcetype: linux_secure")`
`comment("Logic: flags sudo commands that create users, modify group membership, or otherwise grant elevated privileges -- especially from accounts that don't normally perform admin actions")`
`comment("Expected hit in sample data: admin using useradd/usermod to create + elevate svc_backup immediately after the brute-force login")`

index=security_lab sourcetype=linux_secure sudo_user=* command=*
| rex field=command "(?i)(?<priv_action>useradd|usermod\s+-aG\s+sudo|groupadd|passwd|visudo|chmod\s+u\+s|adduser)"
| where isnotnull(priv_action)
| table _time sudo_user target_user command priv_action
| sort - _time

`comment("Tuning: build a lookup of 'known admin accounts' and filter to `NOT sudo_user IN (known_admins)` so only unexpected actors trigger the alert.")`
`comment("Tuning: raise severity automatically if this fires within 15 minutes of a successful login that itself followed failed-login activity (see 02_successful_login_after_failures.spl) -- this chains recon -> access -> escalation into one incident.")`
